<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.1" xml:lang="en-US">
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural">
    <prosody rate="+0%">
      <p id="scene-01">
        <s>StatePort gives AI-assisted work a durable home.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>Your applications keep their own state, history, and continuity — and a managed harness runs the coding agents that help with the work.</s>
        <s>Here is the preview.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-02">
        <s>This is the application you get.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>Open a named project and see what is happening, what needs attention, and what the agent last did.</s>
        <s>Your state files and decisions live here, not hidden inside a session.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-03">
        <s>This is the conversation.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>You can ask the agent for help, but the conversation is only one part of the project.</s>
        <s>StatePort preserves the canonical application state — provider capabilities differ and are explicitly profiled, and the work does not live or die with the chat.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-04">
        <s>This screen shows the project information.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>It helps you see what is ready, what is still being checked, and what is only a test.</s>
        <s>That makes it easier to know what you can trust.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-05">
        <s>And this is the mobile view.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>The same project stays readable on a small screen.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-06">
        <s>This is a local preview made on my computer.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>The software is in private alpha testing, with Codex CLI as the only qualified provider, and you cannot download it yet.</s>
        <s>The point of StatePort is simple: give the work a durable home, supervise the agent, and keep what matters.</s>
      </p>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
